  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Classes",
      "items": [
        "Each invariant is settled, to refine, or to generate; probably settled is not a class",
        "User stories are settled only when final, with no question about their expected result open; revising a story makes every invariant derived from it to refine",
        "A general or ambiguous request needs user stories; a trivial or narrowly technical one does not"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Plan",
      "items": [
        "pm roots the plan: user stories first, then a different pm delegation formalizes the business documents from those final stories",
        "analyst runs on a concrete question derived from an invariant in hand; designer and architect are independent unless one constrains the other",
        "qa is conditional: only when planned, it follows spec and architect when present, consuming the specification, frozen contracts and pm's PRD; the plan then ends spec to qa",
        "More than one lane known: dispatch_commit before the first dispatch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Coherence",
      "items": [
        "Ranks are fixed: the user's directive, then user stories, then business documents, then what derives from them; the higher document stands and only the other lane is re-dispatched",
        "Between equal ranks, decide on the user's directive or verified facts; contradictory user stories are the user's to settle, through their pm when that lane runs with the user",
        "Between qa and spec, spec stands for behavior; an unbacked conflict stays disputed and two failed alignments escalate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Seat restoration",
      "items": [
        "A lane whose specialist cannot run has its seat restored per OPERATIONS, with model and reason; the specialty is never replaced",
        "Lanes that do not consume the missing result keep running; consumers wait on the named gap rather than guessing"
      ]
    }
  ]
